      "title": "Note",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Qwen-Image-Edit-2511 \u2014 instruction edit (baseline)\n\n## The matched set \u2014 change one, change all five\n\n| slot | value |\n|---|---|\n| diffusion model | `qwen_image_edit_2511_fp8mixed.safetensors` \u00b7 **`weight_dtype = fp8_e4m3fn`** |\n| text encoder | `qwen_2.5_vl_7b_fp8_scaled.safetensors` \u2014 `CLIPLoader type = **qwen_image**` |\n| VAE | `qwen_image_vae.safetensors` (already on your disk) |\n| latent | `VAEEncode` of the scaled source \u2014 16-channel |\n| patch nodes | `ModelSamplingAuraFlow(shift=3.1)` **\u2192** `CFGNorm(1.0)`, in that order |\n\n## Two things that are set the way they are on purpose\n\n**Use the Comfy-Org build of this checkpoint, not lightx2v's.** Both are ~19 GB\nfp8 and the filenames look interchangeable. They are not:\n\n| build | scale tensors | ComfyUI core |\n|---|---|---|\n| `Comfy-Org/...qwen_image_edit_2511_fp8mixed` | packaged for ComfyUI | \u2705 |\n| `lightx2v/...fp8_e4m3fn_scaled` | `weight_scale`, no `.scaled_fp8` marker | \u274c **all 840 dropped** |\n\nTested on this box 2026-08-26: the lightx2v build loads with **zero errors**, runs\na full 20 steps, and outputs **pure noise**, because ComfyUI silently discards\nevery scale tensor:\n\n```\nunet unexpected: ['transformer_blocks.0.img_mod.1.weight_scale', ...]   x840\n```\n\nfp8 weights minus their scales are meaningless. ComfyUI detects scaled fp8 by a\n`.scaled_fp8` marker and `scale_weight` naming; lightx2v ships `weight_scale`\nand no marker. Same family of silent failure as invariants 2 and 5 \u2014 it does not\nerror, it just gives you garbage.\n\nThe Lightning **LoRA** from lightx2v is fine \u2014 plain bf16, no scales, applies to\neither base. Only the base checkpoint matters here.\n\n**`weight_dtype = fp8_e4m3fn`, measured not assumed.** On `default` this\ncheckpoint loaded at **38,968 MB** \u2014 a straight fp16 upcast of a 19 GB file, for\nidentical weights. `fp8_e4m3fn` keeps it at ~19 GB. Confirm from the load line:\n\n```\nRequested to load QwenImage\nloaded completely; ..... MB loaded\n```\n\n~19,000 MB correct \u00b7 ~38,000 MB means it upcast.\n\n## `TextEncodeQwenImageEditPlus` is where the image enters\n\nIt is **core** (`comfy_extras.nodes_qwen`) \u2014 you do **not** need\n`Comfyui-QwenEditUtils` or any other custom node for this graph. That matters\nbeyond convenience: under invariant 7, a custom node's `requirements.txt` that\ntouches torch will silently install the CPU build on ROCm and take the whole\ninstall down. Fewer custom nodes is a safety property here.\n\nGive it `clip`, `prompt`, `vae` and `image1`. With `vae` wired it encodes the\nsource into reference latents internally, which is what makes this an *edit*\nrather than a re-generation.\n\n**Feed the same scaled image to both** `TextEncodeQwenImageEditPlus.image1` and\nthe `VAEEncode` driving the sampler. Mismatched sizes between the reference\nlatent and the sampling latent are the documented cause of unexpected crop/zoom.\n`FluxKontextImageScale` snaps to a Qwen-friendly bucket; take its output once and\nfan it out, which is exactly how this graph is wired.\n\n`image2` / `image3` are free multi-reference slots \u2014 a second image to composite\nfrom, a style reference. Left unconnected here.\n\n## The reference method must be applied to BOTH branches\n\n`FluxKontextMultiReferenceLatentMethod` sits on the positive **and** the negative.\nThat symmetry is not cosmetic. CFG computes `neg + scale * (pos - neg)`; if the\ntwo conditionings were built with different reference-latent methods you are\nsubtracting incomparable things, and the result is fine-grained colour speckling\nacross flat areas \u2014 walls, carpet, fur.\n\nMeasured here on 2026-08-26: with the method on the positive only, CFG 4.0 gave\npink/red speckle over the whole frame and a malformed hat. The Lightning graph\nat **CFG 1.0 was unaffected**, because at CFG 1.0 the negative branch is never\nevaluated \u2014 which is exactly why a bug like this hides until you raise CFG.\n\n## Writing the instruction\n\nImperative, describing the change. Not a caption.\n\n- \u2705 `Add a black silk top hat to the dog's head.`\n- \u2705 `Change the dog's collar to red leather, keep everything else identical.`\n- \u274c `a dog wearing a top hat, 8k, photorealistic, sharp focus`\n\n## Steps \u2014 a conflict you should know about\n\nThis ships **20 steps @ CFG 4.0**, per your plan. Your own skill reference\n(`04-model-families.md`) lists **40 steps** for 2511 and 20 for 2509. I have not\nmeasured which is right on this box, so I am flagging it rather than silently\npicking: if edits look under-cooked, 40 is the documented value and the first\nthing to try.\n\nRun ten of these on fixed seeds and keep them \u2014 that is your control group for\nevery later comparison.\n"
      ],
